"r{string, variables}" raw string, doesnt include special characters /...

open files function, file_variable = open()
file types e.g open("files/demo.txt,"r")
r = read, w = write, a = append

read text from a file function, variable = file_variable.read()

loop through line by line in a text file
    for line in file_variable:
        print(line)

closes file when finished, preferred
    with open("files/demo.txt") as f:
        for line in f:
            print(line.strip())

writing to a file
    string_variable = "string"
    with open("files/demo.txt","w") as file_variable:
        file_variable.write(string_variable)


close file function, file_variable.close()


csv files

import csv
files/new_demo.csv, reader = csv.reader(file_variable)
returns a list
when using a csv file it returns the headers, use headers = next(reader)